From 8ee0be4221ca2d091964d36ef140188bf1aefe4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:45:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 234/240] Bugfix: read node loads from the node load array in
 mesh ordering routines [report R. Perry]

`meshInduceSepa()` tested the element load array of the original mesh
and read node loads from it, indexed by node numbers, so that for
meshes with element loads it read far beyond that array, and the
actual node loads were ignored. `hmeshOrderHxFill()` did the same to
compute the variable weights of the halo minimum degree routines.
Meshes read from files are not affected, as `meshLoad()` uses a single
load array for elements and nodes, but meshes built through
`SCOTCH_meshBuild()` have separate arrays.

Node loads are in `vnlotax`. The induced separator mesh now stores them
in its own `vnlotax`, and leaves `velotax` NULL, as its elements are not
weighted.

Add `test_scotch_mesh_order`, which orders meshes built in memory with
the default strategy, and checks that an element load array of unit
loads does not change the ordering.

Refs: SEP-02
